    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0977" n="881" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg881"/>

                <head>No. 395.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christiancy to Mr.
                    Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1, 1879</date>.
                        (Received June 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch No. 11, of the 8th ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am glad to see that the latter substantially approves, in advance, of the views
                    I had expressed to Minister Osborn in mine of the 19th ultimo, of which I sent
                    you a copy in mine of the 20th (No. 15).</p>
                <p>I shall take occasion to communicate to the minister of foreign relations the
                    substance of so much of your dispatch (No. 11) as tends to explain and modify
                    the note of Mr. Gibbs to that minister of April 7th.</p>
                <p>Accept the assurance of the high regard and esteem of your friend, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. P. CHRISTIANCY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
